    "Full API spec": "Paths and types:\n\n- src/main/java/Player.java: public enum Player { X, O; public Player next(); public String toString(); }\n  Semantics: next() returns O when this==X, else X. Stable identity values X and O.\n\n- src/main/java/Move.java: public final class Move { public Move(int row,int col,Player player,int index); public int getRow(); public int getCol(); public Player getPlayer(); public int getIndex(); public boolean equals(Object o); public int hashCode(); public String toString(); }\n  Semantics: Immutable value; index is the 0-based move order at time of append; equals/hashCode based on row,col,player,index.\n\n- src/main/java/GameState.java: public final class GameState { public enum Status { IN_PROGRESS, DRAW, X_WON, O_WON } public Status getStatus(); public java.util.Optional<Player> getWinner(); public static GameState inProgress(); public static GameState draw(); public static GameState won(Player p); public String toString(); }\n  Semantics: inProgress() => status IN_PROGRESS, empty winner; draw() => status DRAW, empty winner; won(X) => status X_WON, winner Optional.of(X); won(O) => status O_WON, winner Optional.of(O). Instances are value-like and may be reused.\n\n- src/main/java/Board.java: public final class Board { public Board(int size); public int getSize(); public boolean isInBounds(int row,int col); public Player getCell(int row,int col); public boolean isEmpty(int row,int col); public boolean setCell(int row,int col,Player player); public void clearCell(int row,int col); public Player[][] snapshot(); }\n  Semantics: size>=5 expected by Game; Board stores grid with null signifying empty. getCell returns null for empty. setCell sets only if in-bounds and currently empty then returns true; otherwise returns false without mutation. clearCell sets cell to null if in-bounds. snapshot returns a defensive deep copy array of Player references (null allowed) reflecting current state.\n\n- src/main/java/WinDetector.java: public final class WinDetector { public static boolean hasFiveInRow(Board board,int row,int col,Player player); }\n  Semantics: Pure function; counts contiguous stones including the just-placed at (row,col) for both signs of the four directions: (0,1),(1,0),(1,1),(1,-1). If any direction yields count>=5, return true; otherwise false. Assumes (row,col) contains 'player'. No mutation; deterministic.\n\n- src/main/java/Game.java: public final class Game { public Game(int size); public Board getBoard(); public Player getCurrentPlayer(); public GameState getState(); public boolean placeMove(int row,int col); public boolean undo(); public void reset(); public java.util.List<Move> getHistory(); }\n  Constructor semantics: if size<5, throw IllegalArgumentException. Initializes a fresh Board(size), currentPlayer=Player.X, state=GameState.inProgress(), and empty history list.\n  getBoard: returns the live Board instance used by the Game (tests may call snapshot for inspection if needed but will use only Game API).\n  getCurrentPlayer: returns the player whose turn it is. Alternation occurs only while state is IN_PROGRESS.\n  getState: returns current GameState.\n  placeMove: Behavior only when state is IN_PROGRESS: if out-of-bounds or occupied, return false with no mutation; otherwise place currentPlayer stone via Board.setCell, append exactly one Move(row,col,currentPlayer,index=historySizeBeforeAppend), evaluate WinDetector.hasFiveInRow; if win, set state=GameState.won(currentPlayer) and DO NOT toggle currentPlayer; else if board is full, set state=GameState.draw(); else leave state=IN_PROGRESS and toggle currentPlayer=currentPlayer.next(). Return true only for a successful placement during IN_PROGRESS. When state is terminal (DRAW or *_WON), any call returns false with no mutation.\n  undo: If history is empty, return false with no mutation; otherwise remove the last Move m, clear that cell on Board, set currentPlayer=m.getPlayer(), set state=GameState.inProgress(), and return true.\n  reset: Clear all board cells; clear history; set currentPlayer=Player.X; set state=GameState.inProgress(); must not derive first player from prior turn.\n  getHistory: returns an unmodifiable view (or defensive copy) of moves in chronological order with indices consistent with append time.\n\n- src/main/java/Main.java: public final class Main { public static void main(String[] args); }\n  Semantics: Construct a Game (e.g., size 15), perform a couple of safe moves per the canonical API, may print at most one concise line like \"Caro core ready\", and return normally. Must not call System.exit.\n\nAllowed import/use directions: Main depends on Game; Game depends on Board, Player, GameState, Move, WinDetector; WinDetector depends only on Board and Player; Domain entities (Player, Move, GameState, Board) have no dependencies on runtime entry. Tests import and exercise only the canonical Game API and Main.main.",
